    "display_name": "Simulating Growth",
    "long_instructions": "**In nature, many animals and plants spread by multiplying—much like the viral social media post you saw in class.**\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Choose an animal or plant whose population growth you’d like to simulate\r\n- Complete `simulate` to simulate the population growing over any number of days.\r\n- Ensure that, for each day, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Day {day}: population of {population}\"`. Start with day 0.\r\n- Choose the starting conditions for your population and call `simulate`.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python’s `for` loop can repeat code a certain number of times. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\niterations = 10\r\nfor i in range(iterations):\r\n    print(i)\r\n```",
